WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.367 --> 00:00:01.134 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Hi, Annie. How are you?

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:03.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hi, Seth.
I am doing just fine.

00:00:03.403 --> 00:00:04.137 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
How are you doing?

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:06.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm doing well.
It's really nice to meet you

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:07.674 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I wish it was in person.

00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:11.011
But I was talking to your costar
Dan Levy,

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:14.381
and he was saying that, really
it's the most fitting outcom

00:00:14.381 --> 00:00:18.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
that the year "Schitt's Creek"
gets 15 nominations,

00:00:18.318 --> 00:00:19.853 size:88% position:44% line:92%
it will be virtual Emmys

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:21.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
because we're in the middl
of a pandemic.

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:25.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Precisely.
I couldn't agree with him more

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:26.659 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:29.896 align:start size:94% position:6%
It must have been -- You know,
your show took this --

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:31.231 line:92%
I feel like had this crazy -

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:34.267
"Arc" isn't even the right wor
because it just kept going up,

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:37.170
which is it was a show tha
not a lot of people saw,

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:40.640
and then there was this building
sort of cult feeling about it,

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then, all of a sudden,
in its final year,

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:43.877 size:81% position:41% line:92%
it is an Emmy darling.

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:46.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
What a fun run that must hav
been for you.

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:49.816 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's been so wild,
because when we started out,

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:54.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
it was really just this little
show on the CBC in Canada.

00:00:54.154 --> 00:00:57.390 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we shot, you know,
in Toronto,

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then we'd go up north
45 minutes

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:03.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
and shoot in this little tow
called Goodwood, Ontario.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:06.132 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's hilarious.

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:07.700 line:92%
-Hold on to that for a sec

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:10.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, yeah, it felt really small
and insular,

00:01:10.537 --> 00:01:17.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
and so, to have it be wher
it is now is pretty wonderful.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:19.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Is it true that
you felt nostalgic

00:01:19.179 --> 00:01:22.882 size:78% position:39%
and made a trip back
to Goodwood recently?

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:24.784 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yep, yep.

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:29.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
It is not my finest moment
I would say.

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:32.992
I was getting a little
stir crazy and nostalgic,

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:35.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was like,
"I'm gonna take a little drive

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:36.729 line:92%
I'm gonna go to Goodwood."

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:37.530 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And they have these --

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:39.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's a bakery in Goodwood
called Annina's,

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:42.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is the best bakery,
and they have --

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:44.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you guys have butter tart
in America?

00:01:44.237 --> 00:01:46.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I've never heard
of a butter tart.

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:49.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, a butter tart
is just that --

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:52.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
a butter tart
but with brown sugar and -

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:52.812 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Anyway, it's delicious.

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:56.382
So I said, "I'm gonna go get
a butter tart and walk around.

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:58.618 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And so I did that,

00:01:58.618 --> 00:02:01.855
and I was strolling around
the streets of Goodwood,

00:02:01.855 --> 00:02:05.792 align:start size:94% position:6%
and this car of ladies
pulls up to me,

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:08.928 line:92%
and they're like, "Alexis?

00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:11.664 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And I was like...

00:02:12.699 --> 00:02:15.168 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"What are you doing here?"

00:02:15.168 --> 00:02:16.536 line:92%
Like, because Goodwood, I guess,

00:02:16.536 --> 00:02:21.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
has become a bit of a hot spot
for tourists now.

00:02:21.741 --> 00:02:22.208 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Sure.

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:25.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But they had driven
three hours

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:27.013 align:start size:94% position:6%
to come and take pictures
in Goodwood,

00:02:27.013 --> 00:02:32.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there I was just wandering
the streets like a maniac.

00:02:32.018 --> 00:02:35.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, literally
three days later,

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:38.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
the show "Schitt's Creek"
posted on socials,

00:02:38.525 --> 00:02:41.895 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Please, people,
stop going to Goodwood.

00:02:41.895 --> 00:02:45.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
There is a pandemic.
Everyone needs to calm" --

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:47.634 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And I was like...

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:49.035 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:49.035 --> 00:02:51.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
It is really funny because
of course, the last --

00:02:51.938 --> 00:02:55.742
I mean, you might expect to see,
like, an Annie look-alike

00:02:55.742 --> 00:02:58.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
that the town just hired
for the purposes of tourists

00:02:58.244 --> 00:03:00.180
but to get the real thing
just wandering around...

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:05.185
-Now I think that they think
that I just go there every day

00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:08.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
just to wait for people
to come and take my picture.

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:08.988 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-To recognize you, sure.

00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:10.390
This is something else that'
a little bit embarrassing,

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:13.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
but, again, this is somethin
that you made the mistake of
sharing with the world,

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:17.330
which is that when you found out
you were nominated
for an Emmy --

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:20.867 size:84% position:42%
this is going around --
you choked on bacon.

00:03:20.867 --> 00:03:23.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
Which is, by the way,
the way I want to imagine

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:26.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
all Canadian actors finding ou
about Emmy nominations,

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:28.308 size:75% position:38% line:92%
is choking on bacon.

00:03:28.308 --> 00:03:30.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was one of those thing
that, like, as I was saying it

00:03:30.843 --> 00:03:33.446 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "Don't say thi
out loud to somebody."

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:38.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, yeah, I was sitting
on the floor eating pancakes

00:03:38.585 --> 00:03:39.953 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
as one does,

00:03:39.953 --> 00:03:41.654 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and got the news

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:47.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
and inhaled or exhaled
in a poor way,

00:03:47.794 --> 00:03:51.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, yeah,
that's how I rung in the news,

00:03:51.698 --> 00:03:53.499 size:78% position:39% line:92%
was choking on bacon.

00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:56.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What -- I can't even imagin
what it was like

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:59.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
to have both comedy royalt
and Canadian royalty

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:02.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
in Eugene Levy
and Catherine O'Hara

00:04:02.242 --> 00:04:02.742 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
as your parents.

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:05.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
What was it like when you firs
started working with them?

00:04:05.345 --> 00:04:07.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, obviously,
the scripts are so funny,

00:04:07.113 --> 00:04:09.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
but, you know,
they elevate it so much

00:04:09.148 --> 00:04:10.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
by being the kind of performer
they were.

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:14.287
Was it intimidating, or was it
just amazing from the start?

00:04:14.287 --> 00:04:17.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Both.
I'm gonna say both.

00:04:17.991 --> 00:04:24.764 align:start size:94% position:6%
They have been my idols
for so many years,

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:28.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
and when I found out
I got the job --

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:30.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because I hadn't
worked for so long,

00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:35.308
teemed with the fact that it
was my dream job that I booked

00:04:35.308 --> 00:04:38.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was, like, floating
on this high

00:04:38.778 --> 00:04:39.812 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
that I had a job

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:41.714
and I was gonna be working
with Eugene and Catherine.

00:04:41.714 --> 00:04:45.918
But I didn't really realiz
until a couple of days befor

00:04:45.918 --> 00:04:50.056
when a friend was like,
"Hey, you have to now act

00:04:50.056 --> 00:04:52.458 align:start size:94% position:6%
with Eugene Levy
and Catherine O'Hara."

00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:57.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like, "Oh, no.
Oh, no, no, no, no."

00:04:57.096 --> 00:05:01.501
And it really dawned on me
and I had a bit of a momen

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:05.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
and was terrified going in
the first day.

00:05:05.004 --> 00:05:06.739 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I was so nervous.

00:05:06.739 --> 00:05:13.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, luckily, Dan Levy
was equally green,

00:05:13.179 --> 00:05:14.647 size:88% position:44% line:92%
and he was nervous, too.

00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:17.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, we kind of went in
trembling together

00:05:17.483 --> 00:05:20.720 align:start size:94% position:6%
and got the first few take
out of the way.

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:24.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then Eugene and Catherine,
being who they are,

00:05:24.691 --> 00:05:26.159 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
it never felt like

00:05:26.159 --> 00:05:29.495
we were the new,
inexperienced kids that we were.

00:05:29.495 --> 00:05:31.564 line:92%
It was so warm and awesome

00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:35.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they couldn't have bee
more lovely, so...

00:05:35.501 --> 00:05:36.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was talking to Dan
about this.

00:05:36.636 --> 00:05:39.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, six years ago,
he and Eugene came on

00:05:39.372 --> 00:05:41.507 size:84% position:42%
to promote the premiere
of "Schitt's Creek,"

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:44.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, at the time,
I think the only thing anyon
knew about the show

00:05:44.744 --> 00:05:48.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
was the choice that
they had made with the name.

00:05:48.147 --> 00:05:50.583 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And it was really fun.

00:05:50.583 --> 00:05:51.751 size:81% position:41% line:92%
One, they obviously --

00:05:51.751 --> 00:05:55.655
You know, the secret's out
that they have a very loving
father/son relationship,

00:05:55.655 --> 00:05:58.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you actually were
in the city doing press,

00:05:58.558 --> 00:06:00.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I've heard that you
actually went --

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:03.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
you went to their hotel room
to watch it air,

00:06:03.262 --> 00:06:05.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is probably
pretty late at night.

00:06:05.398 --> 00:06:07.233 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I did, and it was.

00:06:07.233 --> 00:06:08.935 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I can stay up late.

00:06:08.935 --> 00:06:13.172
Yeah, so that was one of
my very first -- of many -

00:06:13.172 --> 00:06:18.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
but very first moments of
"what is my life right now?"

00:06:18.678 --> 00:06:22.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because I was in New York City
for press,

00:06:22.448 --> 00:06:24.684 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they put us up
at the Waldorf Hotel.

00:06:24.684 --> 00:06:27.653
And we'd just gone out
for this beautiful steak dinner,

00:06:27.653 --> 00:06:30.623 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there was a snowstorm,
and I was like --

00:06:30.623 --> 00:06:32.458 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I was crawling into bed,

00:06:32.458 --> 00:06:34.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I got a call from Dan
being like,

00:06:34.594 --> 00:06:38.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
"We're gonna watch
'Seth Meyers.' Come on up.

00:06:38.765 --> 00:06:39.699 line:92%
And gave me a room number.

00:06:39.699 --> 00:06:43.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, I pulled on
my rumpled clothes

00:06:43.403 --> 00:06:43.903 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and went up.

00:06:43.903 --> 00:06:48.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was, like, an
impressive number in the hotel

00:06:48.508 --> 00:06:53.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, I went up to the roo
and knocked on the door,

00:06:53.179 --> 00:06:58.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Martin Short
dressed in a tuxedo

00:06:58.551 --> 00:07:05.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
opens the door with champagn
and goes, "Annie Murphy."

00:07:05.358 --> 00:07:07.627 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And I was like, "What!?"

00:07:07.627 --> 00:07:13.800 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, I proceeded to go into
Martin Short's hotel room

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:14.834 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
at the Waldorf

00:07:14.834 --> 00:07:20.106 size:75% position:38%
and watch my friends
Eugene and Dan Levy

00:07:20.106 --> 00:07:21.908 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
on "Seth Meyers,"

00:07:21.908 --> 00:07:24.677 line:92%
and it was a very, very --

00:07:24.677 --> 00:07:29.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think it's like a
"flash before my eyes
while I'm dying" moment.

00:07:29.248 --> 00:07:31.284 line:92%
-It also seems very cool,

00:07:31.284 --> 00:07:32.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I think one of
the most special things

00:07:32.919 --> 00:07:35.955
about all the nominations
is that both Eugene and Da

00:07:35.955 --> 00:07:38.458 align:start size:94% position:6%
got nominated,
and I can only imagine

00:07:38.458 --> 00:07:39.692 line:92%
how proud it made Eugene.

00:07:39.692 --> 00:07:43.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, he's got two kid
in the cast, as well.

00:07:43.196 --> 00:07:44.797 line:92%
Is it true that he just delights

00:07:44.797 --> 00:07:46.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
in watching
his children perform?

00:07:46.899 --> 00:07:52.538
-Couldn't be more delighte
watching his kids perform.

00:07:52.538 --> 00:07:52.905 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It is --

00:07:52.905 --> 00:07:56.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
That is actually one of
the things that I'm gonna miss
the very most

00:07:56.075 --> 00:07:58.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
about shooting,
is watching Eugene

00:07:58.177 --> 00:08:01.113 size:75% position:38% line:92%
watch Sarah and Dan.

00:08:01.113 --> 00:08:05.017 line:92%
Because he stands -- He goes -

00:08:05.017 --> 00:08:06.886 align:start size:94% position:6%
First of all,
he goes and gets snacks,

00:08:06.886 --> 00:08:09.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then he stands
behind the monitor

00:08:09.822 --> 00:08:11.324 line:92%
and just watches them act.

00:08:11.324 --> 00:08:16.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he's much like a dance mom
or like a stage mother.

00:08:16.295 --> 00:08:21.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
He mouths their lines and
is very sad when they're sad

00:08:21.701 --> 00:08:23.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
and very happy
when they're happy.

00:08:23.870 --> 00:08:25.137 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And it's all of us.

00:08:25.137 --> 00:08:28.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, when it's going on,
all of the crew kind of
nudge each other,

00:08:28.574 --> 00:08:33.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we all take great pleasure
in watching him watch them

00:08:33.713 --> 00:08:35.515 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-It is fully adorable.

00:08:35.515 --> 00:08:37.583 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I want to ask
about Catherine.

00:08:37.583 --> 00:08:39.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
She made so many
wonderful choices

00:08:39.719 --> 00:08:41.821 line:92%
in her delivery and diction.

00:08:41.821 --> 00:08:43.923 line:92%
Was there a certain word of hers

00:08:43.923 --> 00:08:45.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you enjoyed
hearing the most

00:08:45.525 --> 00:08:47.527 align:start size:94% position:6%
over the course
of the six seasons?

00:08:47.527 --> 00:08:50.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, and it's not the word
you would expect

00:08:50.663 --> 00:08:53.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it's not one of
the flowery,

00:08:53.232 --> 00:08:55.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, pieces of vocabulary
that she chooses.

00:08:55.668 --> 00:09:02.475 align:start size:94% position:6%
But she was able to
make the word "how,"

00:09:02.475 --> 00:09:07.780
just the word "how," just H-O-W,
three syllables.

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:11.851 line:92%
So it went from how to "H-O-W.

00:09:11.851 --> 00:09:13.085 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:09:13.085 --> 00:09:17.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it blew my mind.
It blew my mind.

00:09:17.690 --> 00:09:19.759 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
She's a miracle.

00:09:19.759 --> 00:09:22.628 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Well,
you were very lucky.

00:09:22.628 --> 00:09:24.730 align:start size:94% position:6%
To be that proximity
to greatness

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:26.632 line:92%
is very rare in this game.

00:09:26.632 --> 00:09:30.036 size:84% position:42%
And it's really awesome
that the Emmy voters

00:09:30.036 --> 00:09:31.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
recognized how,
across the board,

00:09:31.871 --> 00:09:34.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
wonderful you all were
on that show.

00:09:34.140 --> 00:09:35.775 line:92%
And congratulations, Annie

00:09:35.775 --> 00:09:39.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you. Thanks, Seth.
It was really nice to meet you

00:09:39.712 --> 00:09:41.247 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-It was the same here.

